1. What is Jenkins?

Jenkins is an open-source automation tool used for Continuous Integration (CI) and Continuous Deployment (CD).

It automatically:

Builds code
Runs tests
Creates packages
Deploys applications
Example Flow
Developer Writes Code
          ↓
Push to GitHub
          ↓
Jenkins Detects Change
          ↓
Build Project
          ↓
Run Tests
          ↓
Deploy Application
2. Jenkins Architecture (Master-Agent Model)

Jenkins follows a Master-Agent Architecture.

Master (Controller)

The master manages:

Web UI
Job scheduling
User management
Plugin management
Agent coordination
Agent (Worker Node)

Agents perform:

Building projects
Running tests
Deployments
Architecture
          Jenkins Master
                |
     -----------------------
     |          |         |
  Agent 1    Agent 2   Agent 3
 (Java)      (Node)    (Docker)

This allows Jenkins to run multiple jobs simultaneously.

