6. Freestyle vs Pipeline Jobs
Freestyle Job

Traditional method.

Configuration done through UI.

Source Code
↓
Build
↓
Test
↓
Deploy
Advantages
Easy
No coding required
Disadvantages
Hard to maintain
Not version controlled
Pipeline Job

Pipeline is written as code.

Stored in repository.

Example:

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo 'Building'
            }
        }
    }
}
Advantages
Version control
Reusable
Easy automation
7. Declarative Pipeline Syntax

Most commonly used.

Example:

pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo 'Building Project'
            }
        }
    }
}
Structure
Pipeline
  ↓
Agent
  ↓
Stages
  ↓
Steps
8. Scripted Pipeline Syntax

More flexible.

Example:

node {
    stage('Build') {
        echo 'Building'
    }

    stage('Test') {
        echo 'Testing'
    }
}
Difference
Declarative	Scripted
Simple	Flexible
Easier	More Coding
Recommended	Advanced Usage
